output.summary:
GLOSS.emanation can't be tested inside the implemented subset. The Rules Glossary is in scope, but no in-scope content creates an Emanation: not the 32 spells (their areas are Cone, Cube, Cube and Sphere), the level 1–3 features of Fighter, Rogue, Cleric and Wizard, the 14 monsters or the 7 magic items. The engine has no Emanation code at all ('emanation' doesn't appear in dungdra/, and geometry.in_area raises for it). This matches the GLOSS.cylinder decision: all four clauses are recorded as out-of-scope, with no tests and no tickets.

When an Emanation creator enters scope (Spirit Guardians, Aura of Protection, …), its tests should build on stage A's proposed readings, which need rulings first:
- the distance is measured from the edges of the origin's space, with the grid metric, inclusive, and a creature counts when the centre of its space is in the area;
- the origin is left out by default, as in R-29 and R-31;
- the creator chooses whether to include the origin once, when the effect is created.

The 'stationary effect' gap also needs a ruling. I added one cheat to loop/abuse-catalogue.md: leaving behind a moving aura or carrying along a stationary one, toggling the origin's inclusion, and measuring a Large origin's Emanation from its centre. Stage B gave no scenario verdicts that need action.
